      "id": "s02",
      "title": "Adjoint method for inverse & Solving linear equations",
      "page": 44,
      "inShort": "Adjoint adj(A) = [A_ij]^T (transpose of cofactor matrix). A⁻¹ = adj(A) / |A| (when |A| ≠ 0). Method of inversion: A X = B ⇒ X = A⁻¹ B. Method of reduction: convert [A|B] to upper triangular form.",
      "sections": [
        "2.2.2 Adjoint Method",
        "2.3 Application of Matrices (Inversion & Reduction)"
