      "kind": "problem",
      "page": 53,
      "text": "Solve the following equations by the method of inversion: x + y + z = 6, x − y + z = 2, 2x + y − z = 1.",
      "answer": "A = [[1,1,1],[1,−1,1],[2,1,−1]], X = [x,y,z]^T, B = [6,2,1]^T.\n|A| = 1(1−1) − 1(−1−2) + 1(1+2) = 0 + 3 + 3 = 6 ≠ 0.\nadj(A) = [[0,2,2],[3,−3,0],[3,1,−2]].\nX = (1/6) adj(A) B = (1/6) [6, 12, 18]^T = [1, 2, 3]^T.\nHence x = 1, y = 2, z = 3.",
